Third-party code

Parts of Misty are adapted from other open-source projects. Each adapted file names its source in
a header, and the notices below are preserved as their licenses require.

desktop-cc-gui (https://github.com/zhukunpenglinyutong/desktop-cc-gui)
  Adapted in src-tauri/features/engines and src-tauri/features/project: the agent engine adapters
  (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, the Agent Client Protocol engines Kimi, Grok, MiniMax, Qoder and
  Oh My Pi, CodeBuddy, Antigravity and Pi), program discovery, and the files, Git, Git-ignore,
  worktree, terminal, open-in-app, HTML preview and clipboard backends (src-tauri/features/project)
  and window state (src-tauri/features/browser/app_windows). The panels beside a chat follow its
  file tree, editor, find and replace, Markdown and HTML preview, changes panel, terminal,
  worktree, open-in and launch-script features and its workspace grouping
  (src/features/agents/context-panel, src/features/agents/engines/enginesApi.ts). The chat composer's `@` file, `/` command, `$` skill and `!` prompt menus and its
  engine command and skill catalog follow its composer
  (src/features/agents/conversations/composer/controls). The chat view adapts its streaming
  Markdown (paced reveal, chunked parsing, cached highlighting), tool payload viewer and edit line
  stats, run status strip, run details and context breakdown, message anchor rail, search inside a
  chat, file links, directory grant card, prompt history and command palette
  (src/features/agents/runs/markdown, src/features/agents/progress/payload,
  src/features/agents/conversations, src/features/commands,
  src-tauri/features/engines/folder_grant.rs). Engine management is adapted in
  src-tauri/features/engine_config and src/features/engine-config: the engines' own MCP servers,
  the skills hub, the prompt library, usage statistics and plan limits, CLI install and update,
  provider channels and CC Switch import, the network proxy, fonts and the performance panel,
  and Pi's per-provider editor (piFamilyModelsBlocks.ts). The notes shown after an update follow
  its upgrade announcement (src/features/updater).
  The safety scan on what an engine writes into memory follows its memory scan
  (src-tauri/features/memory/scan.rs).
  Also adapted: bot bundles and the bot prompt (src-tauri/features/bots, src/features/bots), the
  persona catalog and the composer's `#` menu (src-tauri/features/agent_catalog,
  src/features/agent-catalog), computer use for outside engines and its virtual cursor
  (src-tauri/features/computer_use, src/features/computer-use, src/app/computer-cursor.html),
  desktop pets (src-tauri/features/pets, src/features/pets), and pruning the AppImage's bundled
  Wayland libraries (cli/src/release/appimage.rs).

